\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Needed To Cut Risk Premiums\b0\par\par\uc2 1,232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:28(Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  CDS spreads are one reason \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary, says Hans Redeker, strategist with \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . One way to cut into "the risk premium on the CDS side is to weaken the Japanese yen," he says, adding it would also create more confidence for the economy as domestic demand remains under pressure. Japan's 5-year CDS spread is 6bp wider, from Wednesday, at 110bps, according to Markit. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1527 GMT [Dow Jones] The Monetary Policy Council of Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to judge the monetary policy trend of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and wait for more stability in global markets, before raising rates, says BRE. The MPC will pay more attention to lower-than-expected February CPI and wages and to Thursday's higher-than-expected industrial output data, when it decides on rates in early April, says BRE. February industrial output which came in at +10.7%, would have been a positive surprise for the MPC, which in its March minutes said it was uncertain about the pace of Poland's economic recovery, notes BRE. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:18 (Dow Jones) Citing the recovery of credit card issuers, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  says its outlook for the U.S. credit card industry is stable. Delinquencies and charge-offs have been declining in recent quarters so the improvement trend is likely to continue, says Curt Beaudoin, author of the report. Asset quality has improved as employment fundamentals are better and issuers have charged off bad loans and replaced them with new loans with tighter lending standards. Lending criteria remain high, as well. (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1515 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds started the day in negative territory and have continued to drift lower as stock markets rally, re-couping some of their recent losses. The June contract is 64 ticks lower at 123.01. Bunds are also under pressure from Thursday's Spanish and French multi-tranche bond auctions with in excess of EUR12.5 billion of paper sold. Apart from T-bills, no new paper is expected in Europe until next Wednesday. In the cash market the 2-year bund yields 1.535% and the 10-year 3.145%, flattening the curve by 2 bps to 161 bps. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1456 GMT [Dow Jones] Minutes of the March meeting of the Polish MPC show the council pays more attention to economic growth than to CPI in its policy decisions, says BPH economist Adam Antoniak. Notes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main goal is to ensure stability of prices. The MPC doesn't seem to have a firm opinion about the pace of economic growth and may delay monetary action until new macroeconomic data are released, Antoniak says. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:45 (Dow Jones) Mexico's peso is recovering some of Wednesday's losses as stocks pick up on positive weekly U.S. jobs data. The dollar was recently quoted at MXN12.1115 in Mexico City, according to Infosel, compared with MXN12.1465 at the previous close. The peso's rebound is so far more cautious than the one seen earlier in the week, when it also had depreciated sharply in a single session on worries about the Japan crisis. Japan-related risk remains, and analysts see 12.20-12.21 as a key level to watch in the event of another selloff. (anthony.harrup@dowjones)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 10:41 (Dow Jones) Canadian dollar finds session highs against a broadly weaker U.S. dollar, rising along with equities and the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth-linked peers. U.S. dollar is lower, at C$0.9838, from C$0.9909 late Wednesday, according to data provider CQG. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1435 GMT [Dow Jones] PLN is stronger after industrial output data, with the robust figure for February, +10.7%, adding fuel to monetary policy hawks, says \uc2 Bank Millennium\uc2 . Solid output should be read together with the below-expectations CPI figure for the month, +3.6%, and it's too early to say if rates will for sure go up in April, Millennium says. EUR/PLN is at 4.0753 from 4.0988 late Wednesday. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1416 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  is sticking to its call for the SNB to raise interest rates in mid-June, based on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assessment of the outlook for the Swiss economy, issued earlier Thursday. "Three factors could delay an increase in SNB rates - namely soft economic fundamentals, materially lower inflation data over the next three months, or a material CHF appreciation from current levels," according to economist Reto Huenerwadel. "All eyes will be on the ECB, and in a scenario where it hikes rates in April, we don't expect the SNB to lag in monetary tightening steps," he argues. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:12 (Dow Jones) Special questions within Philly Fed survey show 75% of respondents expect to increase output in second quarter. A hefty 36% plan output gains of more than 5%, says Philly Fed. (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1404 GMT [Dow Jones] This week's Belgium 5-year auction was cancelled due to a combination of market volatility, events in Japan and the announcement of the new ESM bond. When the auction was cancelled, traders bought outstanding Belgium bonds pushing valuations to 'rich' levels. The yield differential between 5-year Belgium and Italy is currently at the wide-end of the recent 50-80 bps range, while in the CDS space, the 10-year Belgium/Italy spread has tightened due to the political crisis in Belgium. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  suggests buying the Belgium 3.75% 2020/Italy 3.75% 2021 spread to pick up 83 bps and take advantage of short-term yield dislocations due to the supply-demand situation. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:03 (Dow Jones) \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  raises its GDP growth estimate for Mexico this year to 4.4% from 4%, citing recent economic momentum and expectations that US growth will accelerate. "Domestic demand will likely have a stronger contribution to GDP growth than in 2010, when growth was fueled by exports, particularly in the first two quarters," the bank says. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  thinks the Bank of Mexico will raise its overnight lending rate target to keep inflation expectations from worsening, with a 25 bps hike to 4.75% either in August or December, instead of waiting until 2012. (anthony.harrup@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2  [ 03-17-11 1128ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110317e73h000ae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
