\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Gains Vs Yen After Japan MOF Says It's 'Ready For Battle'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar spiked higher against the yen Thursday morning, though it still remained down on the day against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after a person familiar with the situation told Dow Jones Newswires that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "ready for battle."\par \par \uc2 The dollar spiked from Y78.74 to Y79.20, as investors were put on alert that the MOF, according to the person, stood ready to possibly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem yen strength.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell late Wednesday in extremely volatile trading to its lowest-ever level against the yen, Y76.25. It recovered some of those losses Thursday, but still remained below the Y80 mark many analysts had thought was Japan's line in the sand for its tolerance of yen strength.\par \par \uc2 Investors are on high alert for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to push down the yen against the dollar. Participants in a conference call among the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations, scheduled for 6 p.m. EDT, are likely to discuss recent volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Another person familiar with the matter told Dow Jones Newswires that G-7 members would be unlikely to complain if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654;\par \par \uc2 bradley.davis@dowjones.com [ 03-17-11 1147ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110317e73h000ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
