\par\par \b \uc2 Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Risk Thins  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Trading, Pushes Out Spreads\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat keeps \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders on edge\par \par \uc2 --Flows light, spreads wide, particularly in yen\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Concerns that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen are making it unusually tough to complete trades in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, traders say.\par \par \uc2 Flows are relatively light, and the gap between the prices where banks buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the yen, is abnormally wide, as traders seek to protect themselves from shocks.\par \par \uc2 "Yen traders everywhere have their crash helmets at the ready," one \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  trader said. Against the current backdrop it may be "difficult to transact 'normal' buy orders [in the dollar against the yen] without spooking the market... liquidity has obviously worsened, and spreads will reflect this," he added.\par \par \uc2 Other London traders agreed that the wide spreads and thin trading conditions are unusually prevalent Thursday after the spectacular demand for the yen drove it to all-time highs against the dollar overnight. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf, as the dollar reached the Y80 level, but it didn't. Now markets are on high alert for the possibility that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may yet try to halt the yen's gains.\par \par \uc2 The tensions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market also come after telling comments from Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda Thursday. "Under thin market conditions there are various speculations and nervous movements," he said. "Based on this, I will closely watch the market situation."\par \par \uc2 The strong yen makes Japanese exports more expensive at a particularly difficult time. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen in September 2010. A G7 teleconference on the situation in Japan is due at 2200 GMT and leading to some speculation of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen from key central banks. Comments so far suggest Japanese officials believe speculators are to blame for the yen's current gains, not repatriation flows back into Japan as some market-watchers believe.\par \par \uc2 At 1302 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y78.84 against the yen after hitting a low of Y76.25 overnight.\par \par \uc2 -By Siva Sithraputhran, Dow Jones Newswires, +44 20 7842 9462;\par \par \uc2 siva.sithraputhran@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Katie Martin contributed to this report.) [ 03-17-11 0928ET ]\par \par \uc2 5008   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110317e73h00093\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
