's fresh food needs are expected to ensure continued strong markets for Australia's meat, dairy and grain exports. (david.rogers1@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0234 GMT [Dow Jones] A target of any \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be to push the USD/JPY above 80.0 and let it stabilize around that level, says Nomura Securities chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Taisuke Tanaka. Still, large amounts of funds are necessary for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fulfill that because hedge-related USD/JPY selling by Japanese exporters is likely to weigh on the pair at 80.00. He also notes joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , U.S. and EU is possible, given the Japan-led equities weakness around the world. He adds after that the crisis is settled, the USD/JPY may stabilize in a 80.00-85.00 band. (takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0231 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares are down 0.4% at 461.48, with selling in select blue-chip stocks on continued concerns over the negative impact from Japan's earthquake. Dealers say sentiment is also low because a government economist predicts banks will continue to maintain high interest rates in the second quarter because inflation is likely to remain high. "Fears of a withdrawal of Japanese investors and high inflation are discouraging many players from entering the market these days," sayd a Hanoi-based brokerage trader. Among leading decliners, \uc2 Bao Viet Holdings\uc2  (BVH.VH) is down 4.9% at VND78,000, Vinpearl (VPL.VH) is down 1.6% at VND63,000 and \uc2 PetroVietnam\uc2  fertilizer (DPM.VH) is down 0.6% at VND36,300. The trader tips immediate support for the main index at 460. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0231 GMT [Dow Jones] Philippine shares are falling as investors continue to fret about the nuclear situation in Japan. The benchmark PSEi is off 1.4% at 3823.19 in light volume. Losers are swamping gainers 91 to 12. "We will probably see more of this weakness until the uncertainty in Japan recedes," says Bernard Avinante, analyst at Wealth Securities. Traders place immediate support at 3800 and resistance at 3900. Among heavyweight losers, SM Investments (SM.PH) is down 1.0% at PHP510.50, property developer Megaworld (MEG.PH) is down 1.4% at PHP2.13, PLDT (TEL.PH) is down 3.1% at PHP2,006, and Metropolitan Bank & Trust (MBT.PH) is down 0.9% to PHP61.20. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0219 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot gold is at $1,389.20/oz, down $12.30 since the New York close. Continuing liquidation on Tocom after the USD/JPY lurched lower Wednesday is putting spot under pressure in a similar pattern to Tuesday's trade as Japan investors move to cash. Tocom February 2012 contract is at Y3,561 a gram, down Y85 and has fallen 6.0% since Friday's pre-earthquake levels, reflecting the stronger yen, while spot gold has fallen 1.6%. \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  says technically gold has important support at $1,376, a break of which would signal a deeper correction to $1,360 or even $1,325. "Strategically, we are bullish, but there is not enough in the overnight price action to buy for anything other than the short term, as we would like to keep open the option of buying a dip to $1,325," the bank says.(james.campbell@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0218 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds are lower after the PBOC raises the size on its routine three-month bills sold in the open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to CNY50 billion (from CNY32 billion last week), the largest since late October. "The sizable bill sale amount indicates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-term efforts to mop up flush liquidity," says a Shanghai-based trader with a local fund. Still, he reckons the unchanged yield on the three-month PBOC bills suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably has no imminent plan to hike the country's interest rates. The Shanghai Stock Exchange government bond index is at 127.21 vs 127.22 at its last close and it's likely to stay in a 127.15-127.21 band. (ming.wang@dowjones.com) [ 03-16-11 2252ET ]\par \par \uc2 0215 GMT [Dow Jones] New Zealand government bond prices are lower, while interest rate swaps are higher after comments by Finance Minister Bill English on debt ahead of the weekly Debt Management Office tender, a local bond trader says. English said the government would have to borrow the majority of the money needed to rebuild Christchurch and would increase borrowing to NZ$300 million a week. The trader says the weekly bond tender was "a mixed bag" after the comments with the successful yield spread reaching 5 bps. "Since the tender they've (bond yields and swaps) all moved higher to reflect where the average was in the tender." The NZ Debt Management Office sold NZ$75 million of bonds due March 15, 2019, at an average yield of 5.22% and NZ$175 million of May 15, 2021, bonds at a average yield of 5.43%. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com) [ 03-16-11 2252ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110317e73h00025\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
