\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 774 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 20:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par JAPAN PUSHES TO TAME PLANT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government renews efforts to tame the nuclear power plant at the center of Japan's nuclear crisis after suffering some delays, even as it waited for results of its attempt to cool pools of hot nuclear waste on the scene with seawater carried by helicopter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCKS CLIMB, LED BY ENERGY AS OIL PRICES RISE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks rebound as bets that rebuilding efforts in Japan could lift energy and industrial companies offsets anxieties around the country's nuclear power crisis. The Dow Jones Industrial Average is up about 100 points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US CONSUMER PRICES RISE ON FOOD, GAS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Americans pay more for food and gasoline in February, but underlying inflation is tame, new data show, letting the Federal Reserve keep its easy-money policies. Idled U.S. workers also file fewer new jobless benefit claims.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF 'READY FOR BATTLE' ON YEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Ministry is being increasingly vigilant against the yen's rise ahead of a teleconference among Group of Seven finance ministers, amid threats of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GADHAFI CALLS CEASEFIRE AS TOUGH UN ACTION LOOMS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Libya's army says it will halt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  starting Sunday to allow rebels to lay down their arms, softening repeated threats by Moammar Gadhafi to crush them, as world powers edges towards adopting tough measures to shut down the strongman's military machine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PROSECUTORS SAY RAJARATNAM HAD DEAL INFO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Galleon founder Raj Rajaratnam had exact details of an impending acquisition of PeopleSupport, a company where he had installed a board member, five days before the deal was announced, according to a phone conversation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FDIC SUES EX-WAMU EXECS AND THEIR WIVES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FDIC sues three former executives of the failed Washington Mutual Bank, along with two of their wives. FDIC seeks $900 million in damages for alleged gross negligence and other failures by the former executives.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GENERAL MILLS\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTED TO BUY PAI'S YOPLAIT STAKE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Mills\f28 \uc2 \f2  is set to buy PAI's 51% stake in French dairy company Yoplait for EUR1.6 billion, a person familiar with the situation says. U.S. food company is one of seven bidders that remain in talks. \f28 \uc2 \f2 PAI Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  declines to comment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FEDEX NET DOWN 3.3% ON STORMS, CHARGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FedEx\f28 \uc2 \f2 's fiscal 3Q profit slides 3.3% to $231 million, or 73c a share, as revenue tops Wall Street's views, but unusually severe winter storms pressure shipping volume and boost costs. Shares up 5% as company raises guidance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLDMAN CEO REPORTEDLY MIGHT LEAVE BY END-2011 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This year could be the final one at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  for Chairman and Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lloyd Blankfein\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Fox Business Network's Charles Gasparino reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Sports \par WEST VIRGINIA TOPS CLEMSON \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 West Virginia beats Clemson 84-76 to move on to the second round of the NCAA tournament. Butler and Old Dominion are locked in a tight one, while Morehead State and Louisville are tied at 33 at halftime.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par The Wall Street Journal \par JAPAN TAXPAYERS SEEN PAYING DAMAGES FROM REACTORS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Once the crisis at Japan's crippled nuclear reactors ends and the time comes to allocate financial responsibility, there is likely to be only one party holding the bag: the Japanese taxpayer. Andrew Dowell and Erik Holm explain.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INFLATION IS SLOWLY CREEPING BACK INTO OUTLOOK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While inflation is unlikely to become rampant, consumers are lifting their inflation expectations, and more businesses are marking up their selling prices to recoup input costs, writes Kathleen Madigan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed Watch \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TWIST HINTED AT QE2'S MODEST MARKET IMPACT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A new look at what the Treasury and Fed achieved when they attempted to push long-term bond yields down during the Kennedy Administration helps explain why the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't appear to be getting all that much out of its current Treasury-buying effort, writes Michael Derby.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCKS CLIMB, LED BY ENERGY AS OIL PRICES RISE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares rebound, led higher by energy as oil prices rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS SNAP 3-DAY RALLY, BUT JAPAN CRISIS REMAINS FOCUS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys are lower, snapping 3-day rally as fear over Japan nuclear crisis eases.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR MOVES HIGHER VS YEN ON REPORT G-7 WILL SUPPORT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar moves higher against the yen after a report that G-7 leaders will support \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE BETWEEN CRISES IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , MIDDLE EAST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude oil advances back above $100 as Japan fears abate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLD FLAT AS TRADERS WATCH JAPAN, EQUITIES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comex gold holds near steady on signs of resilience in other markets. [ 17-03-11 1900GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110317e73h001gf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
