\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: MOF JPY Move Likely, No Foreign Opposition - Nomura\b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0152 GMT [Dow Jones] JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be imminent following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dramatic surge earlier this morning, partly because last week's devastating earthquake and tsunami, as well as the nuclear reactor problems, mean that foreign countries that under normal circumstances would oppose such a move are unlikely to do so now, says Nomura Securities in a research report. "Given the extraordinary circumstances in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there should be no real opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from key global partners, including the U.S, and the eurozone." The house says that the dire circumstances in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  also mean that coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "with potential participation from the Fed, ECB and BOE" cannot be ruled out. "Finally, an announcement of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could potentially be combined with further monetary policy easing measures," despite the fact that the BOJ announced additional easing measures on Monday, Nomura says.\par \par \uc2  The USD/JPY is now at 79.57, off its all-time low of 76.25 tapped earlier in the session. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 17-03-11 0152GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110317e73h0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppic