\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: Japan Finance Minister Noda:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Moves Are Nervous\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from a second finance ministry official in paragraphs six and eight, comments from an analyst in paragraphs 10 and 11, plus more detail on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Arran Scott, Martin Vaughan and Tatsuo Ito \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Thursday he is closely watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying there have been nervous moves in thin trading conditions.\par \par \uc2 "Under thin market conditions there are various speculations and nervous movements," he said. "Based on this I will closely watch the market situation."\par \par \uc2 Taken together with comments by another senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Thursday, the comments show Japanese officials believe speculators are to blame for the yen's volatility, not repatriation flows back into Japan as some have conjectured.\par \par \uc2 That is significant because \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 -watchers believe officials are more likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to head off a dramatic rise in the yen if they believe that the move is being driven by excessive speculation. Economists and traders said early Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be imminent.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar hit a record low against the yen in late New York trading Wednesday of Y76.25. The dollar later rebounded and was lately changing hands at Y79.34.\par \par \uc2 "It's wrong to think that the yen's sharp rise has been driven by Japanese institutional investors repatriating funds to Japan," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Rintaro Tamaki said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Tamaki is the top bureaucrat in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Japan's finance ministry, which oversees the country's yen policy. He said Japanese institutional investors have sufficient yen cash already, meaning they don't need to sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Instead of selling their foreign investments to bring yen back home, "some institutional investors say they consider this to be a good opportunity to purchase foreign bonds," Tamaki said.\par \par \uc2 Asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister Noda said, "I will not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 But bank economists believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in at any time to restrain the yen. The key question for Japanese officials is picking a time to surprise the market, which isn't "an easy task," said \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  chief Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Masafumi Yamamoto.\par \par \uc2 Japan may want to conduct massive yen-selling that would greatly exceed last September's Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or may want to seek joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the U.S. and Europe, or even ask G-7 or G-20 member nations to release a statement expressing worries, Yamamoto added. It is possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might wait to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until after Tokyo trading hours, in order to surprise traders, he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Arran Scott, Martin Vaughan and Tatsuo Ito, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2770; arran.scott@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Takashi Mochizuki contributed to this report. [ 17-03-11 0109GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110317e73h0002b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
