\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Exporters Tumble;  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  Eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 01:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0055 GMT [Dow Jones] Exporter shares are sharply lower as circumstances at Japan's troubled nuclear power plants remain uncertain, raising expectations for further yen repatriations, which in turn pushed down USD/JPY to record levels before the market open, says Fumiyuki Nakanishi, general manager at SMBC Friend Securities. \uc2 Sony\uc2  (6758.TO) is down 4.5% at Y2,416, Canon (7751.TO) is down 5.8% at Y3,380 and \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2  (7203.TO) is down 4.2% at Y3,205. "The focus now is on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he says. "Firms are now closing books for the fiscal year; the dollar below Y80 is not desirable." He adds that the stock market weakness could be partially alleviated if the Bank of Japan further expands its exchange-traded fund (ETF)-buying limit. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 17-03-11 0055GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5011 55117   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110317e73h0001m\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exc